WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.030
In Hollywood, you're only ever as good as
your last film.

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:06.660
Even if you've been churning out hits for
years on end, all it takes is one awful movie

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:07.799
to take you down a peg.

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:11.519
Here's a look at some awful films that put
an end to an actor's hot streak.

00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:12.700
Serena

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.609
When Jennifer Lawrence stumbled up to the
podium to collect her Best Actress Oscar for

00:00:16.609 --> 00:00:21.570
2012's Silver Linings Playbook, she was already
several films into a hot streak.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:26.109
She'd turned in an impressive performance
in 2010's Winter's Bone and made her first

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:30.260
appearances in the Hunger Games and X-Men
franchises after that, which collectively

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.780
brought in over half a billion dollars.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:36.790
She got her third Oscar nomination for her
scene-stealing role in American Hustle in

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:42.660
2013 and continued to make the whole blockbuster
thing look easy the following year with Mockingjay:

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:43.660
Part 1.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:47.140
"Like I said, I know exactly what I have to
do." (Hopefully it's stop starring in X-Men movies)

00:00:47.149 --> 00:00:53.100
Unfortunately, her streak ended in tame fashion
in 2014 with the universally panned Serena,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.950
which was rejected by audiences, critics,
and even film distributors.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:02.560
After a very limited domestic release which
netted under $200,000, Serena disappeared.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.860
Despite an Academy nod for Joy, the final
Hunger Games film turned out to be the lowest-earning

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:09.850
of the lot, and Lawrence's pull has wavered
ever since.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:11.170
The Great Wall

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:16.100
American movie studios have known for a while
that China's box office has been growing exponentially,

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.790
and some have attempted to take advantage
of the Chinese market by altering their movies

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:22.180
to cater to overseas sensibilities.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:26.189
Others have sought co-productions with Chinese
studios, which is how Matt Damon's The Great

00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:28.080
Wall came to be.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.380
Legendary teamed up with the China Film Group
for what turned out to be an epic disappointment,

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:35.100
grossing $45 million stateside.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.880
Director Zhang Yimou brought plenty of his
famed visual flair to the movie, but it was

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.060
critically trashed, both in the U.S. and in
China.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:46.170
The critical reaction wasn't good for Damon,
who had been on a real hot streak with roles

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:51.440
in Interstellar and The Martian, as well as
a producer credit on Manchester By The Sea.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.860
Things haven't exactly been going great for
Damon since.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:59.390
He saw out 2017 with Suburbicon and Downsizing,
two bizarre comedies that premiered to mixed

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.000
reviews at best.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.860
The Ladykillers

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:06.720
Not many actors can claim to have experienced
a hot streak as long as the one Tom Hanks

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.479
enjoyed for the better part of 15 years.

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:14.080
From the early 1990s to the midpoint of the
2000s, Hanks was a guaranteed draw at the

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:18.470
box office, with his movies rarely pulling
in less than $100 million.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:22.440
In that space of time, he starred in such
critically acclaimed hits as Philadelphia,

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:27.010
Forrest Gump, Apollo 13, Saving Private Ryan
and many, many more.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:31.330
"Somebody later told me it gave people hope.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.330
Nah.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.720
Nah, I don't know anything about that."

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:40.120
It had to happen sometime, but when Hanks'
bubble did eventually burst, it was unexpected.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:43.330
Nobody saw his hot streak coming to an end
with The Ladykillers.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:47.780
The idea of Hanks collaborating with the Coen
brothers on this 2004 remake of a British

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:51.069
classic seemed like a surefire recipe for
success.

00:02:51.069 --> 00:02:55.900
That wasn't the case, however: The movie barely
recouped its $35 million budget in the domestic

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:59.340
box office and was panned by many of the industry's
top critics.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:00.950
The Monuments Men

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:05.340
He hasn't been able to hit that $100 million
mark quite as often as Tom Hanks, but George

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.120
Clooney is also known to bring in the big
bucks on occasion.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:13.530
He generated major bank fronting Steven Soderbergh's
popular and highly profitable Ocean's movies,

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:18.690
and his starring role in the critically-panned
1997 Batman and Robin still managed to bring

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.560
in a cool $238 million.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:28.330
In the late 2000s Clooney was undeniably A-list,
but in 2014 his career took a severe nosedive.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:33.000
Clooney co-wrote, produced, directed and starred
in World War Two caper The Monuments Men,

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:38.090
a story about a rag-tag platoon sent into
Nazi Germany to retrieve stolen works of art.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:42.560
Despite an all-star cast that included Matt
Damon, Bill Murray, and John Goodman, the

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:45.349
movie bombed in theaters and took a licking
from the critics.

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:49.180
Worse, because Clooney was so involved in
the movie's production, there were few other

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:52.310
people to blame besides the former Batman.

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:54.030
Free State of Jones

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:57.560
Matthew McConaughey's career is a tale told
in two acts.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:01.191
After years of depending on his looks and
charm to pay the bills with rom-com after

00:04:01.191 --> 00:04:05.650
forgettable rom-com, he decided to start acting
again, and Hollywood welcomed him back with

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:06.760
open arms.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:12.060
Dubbed the "McConaissance" at the time, McConaughey's
turnaround can be traced back to 2011's The

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.360
Lincoln Lawyer, which scored highly with critics.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:19.410
Between his 2014 Best Actor win for Dallas
Buyers Club and his scene-stealing performances

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:23.580
in The Wolf of Wall Street and Interstellar,
McConaughey seemed unstoppable.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:28.530
Unfortunately, you can't keep making good
choices forever, and McConaughey's 2016 Free

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.290
State of Jones was definitely not a good one.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:36.090
The Civil War drama only managed to claw back
half of its $50 million budget, and the majority

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:37.620
of critics were unimpressed.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:42.890
Worse, his starring turn in 2017's The Dark
Tower was similarly disliked, spelling the

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:45.190
end of McConaughey's box office domination.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:51.210
"No matter who crosses the finish line first,
the universe will die out eventually.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.580
Death always wins." (Except when it comes to bad movie adaptations of great books.)

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.030
King Arthur: Legend of the Sword

00:04:55.030 --> 00:05:00.139
In 2002, Charlie Hunnam starred as Nicholas
Nickleby in a critically acclaimed adaptation

00:05:00.139 --> 00:05:06.060
of the classic Dickens novel and then showed
his darker side in 2005's Green Street Hooligans.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:10.270
Later appearances in Children of Men, Sons
of Anarchy, and Pacific Rim built Hunnam into

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.590
a star to watch.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:15.710
Hunnam followed up the Guillermo del Toro
blockbuster with another del Toro movie, Crimson

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:18.430
Peak, and later, the critically lauded Lost
City of Z.

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:21.400
Unfortunately, his luck was about to run out.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:25.650
With Hunnam as the face and director Guy Ritchie
at the helm, King Arthur: Legend of the Sword

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:29.770
was supposed to be the start of new franchise
based on the legendary character.

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:33.870
Those plans were hastily scrapped after the
box office numbers spelled disaster.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:39.020
Warner Bros. signed off on a $175 million
budget, but the film made less than $40 million

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.430
domestically.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:44.610
It looks like in this case, Hunnam wasn't
quite worthy to take the sword from the stone.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:50.199
"Anyone can pull it once it's been pulled."

00:05:50.199 --> 00:05:51.199
Thanks for watching!

00:05:51.199 --> 00:05:53.460
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:55.779
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

